    "narrative": "Our optimal lineup for today, 2026-07-29, is headlined by **James Wood**, who commands the highest score of the day at 74.28. Facing Yesavage, **James Wood** benefits from an elite 0.425 xwOBA and the leadoff spot, making him the premier cornerstone for our Roto categories. **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) also stands out as a high-floor play; his favorable matchup against Rodriguez (5.28 xERA) and the benefit of a projected three-hole spot provide a massive boost to our power and RBI potential. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first philosophy, utilizing the 10% leadoff bonus for **Brice Turang** (63.55) and **Cole Young** (63.25), both of whom are positioned to exploit Lauer\u2019s struggling peripherals.\n\nThe decision to bench **Edwin Arroyo** (47.65) was our most difficult call, as he narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient profiles of our active infielders. While **Edwin Arroyo** offers switch-hitting versatility, his projected eighth-place spot in the order significantly suppressed his value compared to **Travis Bazzana**, whose presence in the heart of the order provides a more reliable path to counting stats. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley** (47.75), whose utility is tempered by a 45% rain risk and a difficult draw against a pitcher with a 3.79 xERA. If the weather clears, we expect him to outperform his baseline, but we are prepared to monitor the skies until first pitch.\n\nBeyond the core starters, we are looking for **Tyler Soderstrom** (64.04) and **Henry Bolte** (58.36) to take advantage of favorable park factors that inflate their daily efficiency. While **Gabriel Moreno** (49.26) and **Dalton Rushing** (45.53) face tougher pitching, their respective wind-out scenarios and base-running opportunities\u2014particularly **Dalton Rushing** facing a slower delivery\u2014keep them firmly in the mix. Despite the strength of our bench, including **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak**, the current distribution of projected efficiency dictates a full fade of these options to protect our game caps. We remain without **Vinnie Pasquantino** due to his stint on the IL, but the depth of our outfield and utility rotations provides sufficient coverage for today\u2019s slate.",
